  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sealed vessel contains a mixture of two ideal gases, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span>, in thermal equilibrium. The mass of a molecule of gas <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{9}\"></span> of the mass of a molecule of gas <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{v_A}{v_B}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> represents the root-mean-square (rms) speed of the molecules?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"9\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{9}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
